```ts
import type { AnimationGroup, AnimationGroupMask } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function restoreMask(group: AnimationGroup, saved: AnimationGroupMask): void {
    group.mask = {
        mode: saved.mode,
        names: [...saved.names],
        disabled: saved.disabled,
    };
}
```

I assigned a freshly constructed mask object (with a copied `names` array) to `group.mask`, which is all the library needs: note 38 confirms it writes rest values for masked-out nodes and note 40 confirms that replacing the reference (rather than editing in place) is what makes the change visible. I'm not sure of anything — the API surface and the notes together make the requirement unambiguous.
